    "label": "VISPARAD    II.  339 / VISPARAD    III.  34I / VISPARAD    III. / VISPARAD    IV.  343; lines 18651-18792",
    "start": "18651",
    "end": "18792",
    "translation": "The Zend-Avesta, Part III: The Yasna, Visparad, Afrinagan, Gahs, and Miscellaneous Fragments",
    "notes": "Stable markdown line range generated from canonical text."
  },
  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "Liturgical sections of Visparad IV–VII describe the summoning of Mazdayasnian chiefs, warriors, husbandmen, fire-priests, and divine beings such as the Bounteous Immortals and Saoshyants. Dialogues between the Zaotar and Ratu establish priestly announcing and speaking roles. The text offers sacrifices to thoughts, wisdom, sanctity, religious knowledge, health, and the entire holy creation, and references specific offerings like the Myazda-offering and Ratufriti. A priestly speaker approaches the Bounteous Immortals as praiser and invoker, offers even the flesh of his body and the blessings of his life, and confesses faith in Ahura Mazda as a Mazdayasnian of Zarathustra’s order. Further sections describe calling the Amesha Spenta and worshiping the Bounteous Immortals by their beautiful names with ritual Order and Righteousness. The worship extends to sacrificial words, Sraosha, Ashi, Nairya-sangha, victorious Peace, the Fravashis of the saints, the Tsfinva Bridge, and Garo Nmana (Heaven, the best world of the saints). Finally, sacrifices are made to a better path leading to that Best World and worship is given to Arstat (Justice), identified with the Mazdayasnian Faith and helping settlements flourish, together with Rashnu the most just.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The ritual speakers summon chiefs of the Mazdayasnians, the Bounteous Immortals, the pious Saoshyants described as prophets for help, Fire-priests, warriors, and the diligent husbandman of the Mazdayasnian Faith.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The Bounteous Immortals are described as most correct and truthful in speech, most zealous, most glorious in thoughts, the greatest ones, and powerful.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The Saoshyants are explicitly called pious prophets who are summoned for help.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Fire-priests, warriors, and the diligent husbandman are grouped as categories of followers within the Mazdayasnian Faith who are summoned during the ritual.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Atarevakhsha, described as announcing, is said to speak forth to the Zaotar, who is referred to as an Ahu to be revered and chosen.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "The Ratu is called upon to speak forth from his righteousness and is described as holy and learned.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "The Zaotar declares that he will come as this Zaotar and recite the Staota Yesnya with memorised intoning, chanting, and praise.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The worshipers sacrifice to the thoughts of the mind, to good wisdom, to good and blessed sanctity, to good religious knowledge, and to good health of soul and body.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Confession is said to be made for the Kine.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Zarathustrian Mazdayasnians celebrate at the sacrificial time for the Myazda-offering and at the time for the Ratufriti, described as prayer for blessings, and perform sacrificial worship, homage, propitiation, and praise of the entire creation of the holy and clean.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "A priestly speaker approaches the Bountiful Immortals as praiser priest, invoker, memoriser, reciter, and chanter for Their sacrifice, homage, propitiation, and praise, and also in relation to the Saoshyants’ preparation, prayer for blessings, sanctification, and victorious smiting of foes beneficial for their souls.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:4"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "The speaker states that he offers to the Bountiful Immortals the flesh of his very body and all the blessings of his life.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:5"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "The speaker confesses belief in Ahura Mazda and identifies himself as a Mazdayasnian of the order of Zarathustra, in accordance with Zarathustra’s Faith.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:6"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "The speaker calls the good Amesha Spenta by their names of beauty and worships the Bountiful Immortals by their beautiful names, with blessings of ritual Order and Righteousness the good.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:7"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "The ritual is described as being performed with Zaothras intelligently offered and with sacrificial words correctly spoken.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:7"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "The worshipers venerate sacrificial words correctly uttered, Sraosha (Obedience) the blessed, good Ashi (the blest order of rites), Nairya-sangha, and victorious Peace, and they sacrifice to the Fravashis of the saints, to the Tsfinva Bridge, and to the Garo Nmana of Ahura, described as Heaven, the best world of the saints, shining and all-glorious.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:8"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:17",
      "text": "The worshipers sacrifice to a better path that leads to that Best World and worship Arstat (Justice) the good, which helps settlements advance and flourish and is identified as the Mazdayasnian Faith, together with Rashnu, described as the most just.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:9"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:18",
      "text": "The Bountiful Immortals are further described as those who rule aright and dispose of all aright.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:5"]
    }
  ],
