    "summary": "The speaker prays that Sovereign Power beneficial at every hour may be produced, and asks the Great Creator, Righteous Order, and personified Piety for two blessings: sovereign rule over desired wealth and spiritual benefits for worship through Good Mind. He says he speaks for all who are guarded in their actions by the divine law and inspired words from Good Mind speaking through the Mathra, and that these people assemble to hear Ahura Mazda as their foremost guide and light. They cry out asking where their promised lord of thrift stands to show mercy, and where Righteousness, Bountiful Aramaiti (Piety), Best Mind, and Sovereign Power are coming from. A tiller of the earth, described as Ahura’s chosen saint, asks how to obtain the sacred Kine and wealth in herds, motivated by Righteous Order and humble worship of the righteous ruler who appointed a just controlling guide for his creatures. In response, the speaker declares that Ahura Mazda, not a false god of the Daevas, is the one who gives the good citizen gifts better than the good according to religious choice, through divine Authority, and that one who withholds sacrifice will receive worse than evil, including at the last turning of creation. The speaker then asks bountiful Spirit Mazda, creator of the Kine, waters, and plants, for Immortality and Welfare—two eternal powers—through Good Mind and revealed doctrine. He promises that, having these gifts, he will speak for Mazda, declaring what is woe for the wicked but salvation for the one who maintains the holy Order, who is repaid in his deed and rejoiced by the Mathra’s proclamation to the wise. Finally, he vows to declare the mental keenness that reaches decisions, which Mazda has bestowed upon two striving sides through his satisfying word.",
