      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Those guarded by the law assemble to hear Ahura Mazda, who is called their foremost guide and light.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The assembled worshippers cry aloud to Mazda asking where the promised lord of thrift stands to show mercy.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "The worshippers ask from which direction Righteousness, Bountiful Aramaiti (Piety), Best Mind, and Sovereign Power are approaching to inspire, guide, and defend them.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "The lord of thrift is described as an embodied law that saves from dreaded dangers and governs ready zeal.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "A tiller of the earth seeks to gain the sacred Kine and all wealth in herds beside.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "The tiller of the earth asks Ahura how he may gain the sacred Kine, moved by motives flowing from Righteous Order and Ahura’s cause.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "The tiller of the earth is described as upright in actions and wise in self-humbling worship.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "A righteous ruler is said to have appointed a just controlling guide for those whom he has made.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "It is declared that the one who gives the good citizen that which is better than the good, in accordance with his religious choice, is Ahura Mazda.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "Ahura Mazda is contrasted with a false god of the Daevas.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:17",
      "text": "Ahura Mazda bestows good gifts through His divine Authority, while sending worse than evil on the withholder of sacrifice who offers nothing to His cause.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:18",
      "text": "The punishment for withholding sacrifice is said to occur not only in the present but also in the last turning of creation in its course.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:19",
      "text": "Mazda is said to have made both the Kine and the waters and the plants for the Kine’s support.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:20",
      "text": "Immortality and Welfare are described as two eternal powers that Mazda can grant.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:21",
      "text": "Immortality and Welfare are requested through Mazda’s Good Mind in the doctrine revealed by inspired words.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:22",
      "text": "The speaker promises that having Immortality and Welfare in store he will speak for Mazda.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7",
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:23",
      "text": "The speaker says that to a man of understanding one should declare for Mazda that which is woe to the wicked but salvation to the one who has maintained the holy Order.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:24",
      "text": "The man who maintains the holy Order is described as repaid in his deed and rejoiced by the Mathra that declares this to the wise.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:25",
      "text": "Mathra is presented as a proclamation that declares woe and salvation and rejoices the wise.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8",
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:26",
      "text": "Mental keenness that reaches decisions is said to be bestowed by Mazda upon two striving sides in His satisfying word.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:27",
      "text": "A translator’s note remarks that abstract concepts such as Righteousness and Aramaiti are personified in this passage, as elsewhere in the Gathas.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    }
