    "quote": "Yea, I will declare the world's two first spirits, of whom the more bountiful thus spake to the harmful.",
    "summary": "A first-person religious speaker addresses an audience who have come from near and far seeking knowledge. He vows to speak and declares that a false teacher will not kill their life again, and that the wicked are confined by their own faith and speech. He then announces he will reveal the world's two primordial spirits: one more bountiful, one harmful, whose thoughts, commands, understandings, beliefs, deeds, consciences, and souls are entirely opposed. The speaker proclaims that he will set forth the world's first teaching, received from the all-wise deity Mazda Ahura, warning that those who do not obey this Mathra will find their end of life in woe. Finally, he declares the world's best being: Mazda, acting through Righteousness, has appointed things and knows the truth of what he utters, and is described as the father of the toiling Good Mind within humans.",
