    "summary": "Translator's commentary for Yasna XLVIII.153 discusses fear of anarchy under an Evil Authority, the search for a champion-chief who will establish peace \"through blood\" and be aided by coadjutors inspired by the light of reason and true faith. It identifies a single class of human combatants to oppose the Demon of furious Rapine: the saving Saoshyants, vicegerents of the Immortals on earth, including religious princes Vfolaspa, Gamaspa, Frashaartra, and especially Zarathurtra Spitama as Ratu appointed by Ahura for kine and men, called the first tiller, warrior, and priest. The translated verses then describe a saint offering gifts according to Righteous Order who will smite the Demon-of-the-Lie when a long-proclaimed deceitful event comes in Immortal life, blessing men and afflicting Daevas, and a faithful worshipper who increases the Lord's praise and blessings for His folk. The speaker prays to Ahura to reveal the end and grant strength before conflicts or crises encounter him as leader of God's tribes, asking whether the champion of the holy Order will smite the evil heretic and when, calling this the one good consummation of life. A further verse praises the beneficent Ahura's teachings through holy Order and intelligence, along with secret sayings declared by others, and speaks of a chieftain \"one like Thee\" endowed with Good Mind's understanding thoughts. Footnotes explain that the \"conflicts\" can mean crises represented under the figure of a Bridge, the last great crisis for every person, and discuss whether the chieftain is a servant of Ahura or Ahura Himself.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
