    "summary": "This Visparad passage is a litany attached to the Yasna Haptanghaiti. It praises a helpful holy being associated with the recitation of the Yasna Haptanghaiti and describes the text itself as great, powerful, victorious, and free from malice, with its words pronounced for Ahura Mazda's Fire. Visparad XVI enumerates objects of worship and sacrifice: Ahura Mazda's Fire (called his son), Yazads and Rashnus bearing the 'seed of fire', the Fravashis (spirit aspects) of saints, Sraosha who smites with victory, holy men, the entire holy creation, Blessedness and the Fravashi of Zarathustra Spitama, the saints' Fravashis inside and outside the Province, and the Fravashis of holy men and women devoted to the Faith. Sacrifice is offered to those whose service in the Yasna Ahura Mazda is considered best, with Zarathustra as living chief and master, and to fields, waters, lands, plants, and even to the chapters, metred lines, words, and word-structure of the Yasna Haptanghaiti.\n\nVisparad XVII affirms striving after the good thoughts, words, and deeds inculcated in the Yasna Haptanghaiti and defines 'Right (called) the Best' or 'Righteousness Best' as a blessing and source of weal when one is rightly aligned with it. Visparad XVIII describes worship of Ahura Mazda with a specific formula (mta), the Amesha Spenta with another (usta), the holy man, the 'prior world of the holy and clean', and 'the state of weal and salvation for the holy man.' It continues with worship of a lifelong state of blessedness for the holy which is the evil man's calamity, and his eternal salvation, accompanied by a salvation prayer; sacrifice is offered to every saint who exists, is coming into existence, and will exist. \n\nVisparad XIX proclaims worship of Ahura Mazda the bountiful and the Bountiful Immortals, sacrifice to a bountiful saint and to bountiful anticipative understanding, to the good and bountiful Aramaiti (ready mind), and worship of her together with bountiful creatures of the pure creation. Sacrifice is offered to holy creatures whose first attribute is intelligence, and omniscient understanding is worshipped together with Ahura Mazda Himself. The litany then sacrifices to the shining sun, 'highest of the high', worshipped with the Bountiful Immortals and Mathras with good ceremonies, and to glorious achievements, gained glory, and herds that have the Fire and its blessings. Finally, holy benefit that is widely diffused and wisdom identified with the bounteous Aramaiti—whose are the laws of the Righteous Order and of holy creatures with Righteousness as their first attribute—are worshipped.",
    "language": "English",
